# This static frontend (public/index.html) has no build step, so it does
# NOT read a .env file at all — WORKER_URL is a plain constant near the top
# of the <script> tag in public/index.html, set directly in the code.
#
# Real secrets for this project live in exactly two places, neither of
# which is a .env file committed to git:
#
#   1. Cloudflare — Worker (merosadak) → Settings → Variables and Secrets:
#        TOMTOM_API_KEY
#        OPENWEATHERMAP_API_KEY
#        GEMINI_API_KEY
#        WAZE_FEED_URL
#        UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL
#        UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN
#
#   2. GitHub — repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions:
#        FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_MEROSADAK
#
# worker/.env.example documents the two Cloudflare keys that map to actual
# `wrangler secret put` commands. This file is just a map of where things
# live — there is nothing to fill in here.
